---
title: Icteridae
---
# Icteridae

Icteridae is the New World blackbird family, taking in the grackles, the
cowbirds, the meadowlarks and the American orioles. The bill is conical and
sharply pointed, and the family feeds by gaping: the closed bill is driven into
turf or a curled leaf and then forced open. Habits vary enormously, from
cowbirds that lay in the clutches of other species to the orioles, which plait a
deep pouch for their eggs and sling it from a branch tip so that it swings free.
See [[baltimore-oriole]].
